course: dictionary
lesson: 6541
title: New, and what it can mean
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word new is small, but it has several meanings. Look at the words around it to find the right one. «A boy in Halifax squints at the board, and with new glasses the letters are sharp again.» Here new means just made or just bought, because the glasses have not been used before.
explain: New can also mean just arrived or just started. «Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers.» Here new means a medicine that has only just been made and has not been sold before. Ask yourself: is this thing just made, just arrived, or different from before?
explain: Some phrases have their own meaning. «What's new?» is casual talk that means how are you, or what has happened lately. «Brand new» means very new. Always check the whole phrase before you decide what a single word means.
fact: New means just made, just bought, or not used before.
fact: New can mean just arrived or just started, like a new pupil or a new friend.
fact: New can mean different from the one before, like a new start.
fact: «Brand new» and «spanking new» mean very new.
fact: «What's new?» is casual talk that means how are you, or what has happened lately.
fact: «Pre-owned», «pre-loved» and «nearly new» are polite words for used or second-hand.
exercise: «A boy in Halifax needed new glasses to see the board.» What does new mean here? | Old and worn out | Broken and useless | Lost in the classroom | *Just made or just bought, not used before
exercise: «Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers.» What does new mean here? | Very old and famous | Given away for free | *Just made and not sold before | Very cheap
exercise: Your friend says «What's new?» What is she asking? | Are you new to this class | Which toy is the newest | Where is the new shop on the corner | *How are you, and what has happened lately
test: «He is the new kid in our class.» What does new kid mean? | A kid who has new clothes | A kid who is very old | A kid who is famous at school | *Someone who has just started
test: In «8 additional pupils were admitted», additional is a formal word that means which everyday word? | Old | *New or extra | Sad | Lost
exam: Which polite word means second-hand? | Old | *Pre-loved | Broken | Lost
